%erg 0.1
Title: Promote the sitter from bench/ to a top-level plugins/ directory
Created: 2026-09-06
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-06T00:00Z claude created

2026-09-06T09:05Z claude note Heads-up from 0688: bench/check_sitter_version.py pins SITTER = 'bench/sdt-sitter' and walks the history of that path. The move must update it AND keep the old path in the history query (pass both pathspecs), since a rename across a directory is not followed by default and a bare rename would leave the guard reading an empty history, reporting green on no evidence. The same rename applies to the SITTER constants in tests/sdt_sitter_startup.mjs, tests/test_sdt_sitter.py, tests/test_check_sitter_version.py, the docstring of bench/sdt_sitter_install.py, the sitter-version and sitter-install and sitter-verify-install Make targets, and manifest.json's update_url, which now names the raw path bench/sdt-sitter/update.json on main.
2026-09-06T18:39Z claude note Moved. The gate held: 0688-0696 are all merged (0693 landed as PR #388 and stayed open only for the accessibility item it hands to 0686), no remote branch survives the wave, and nothing has touched a sitter path in any worktree. The 0688 heads-up was the whole of the risk and half a fix would have looked like a whole one: widening the `git log` pathspec alone lists the pre-move commits and then skips them as manifest-less, so the revision count comes back as if they had never been listed. Both halves shipped as `HOMES`, and the new arm in tests/test_check_sitter_version.py asserts the literal count; all three mutants (show-only, log-only, neither) were run and all three redden it. The guard now compares against 58 revisions of plugins/sdt-sitter. Two consequences beyond the rename: manifest.json's update_url named the old raw path, and editing a delivered file under an unchanged number is exactly what the guard refuses, so 0.2.11 -> 0.2.12; and check_progress.py's repo-path roster is hand-listed, so `plugins` was added to it. The payload directory is now defined once, in build_sdt_sitter.py, and imported by the guard. The three Python tools stay in bench/ deliberately: test_guard_completeness.py derives its inventory from `bench/check_*.py` and test_check_models.py sweeps `bench/*.py`, so moving them drops them out of both sweeps silently. Their register is a separate question. Verified: `make check` green, 1035 passed / 14 skipped against a 1048-test baseline plus this ticket's one new test; `git log --follow` reaches 5572dcf.
--- body ---
## Context

DECISIONS.md, 2026-09-06 (RATIFIED): the sitter's permanent home is this
repo, not a separate one. `bench/sdt-sitter/` is the wrong register for
something with its own manifest, version, and install lifecycle -- `bench/`
is for probes and one-off measurement scripts. Move the source to a new
top-level `plugins/sdt-sitter/`, echoing README's own theory-of-change
vocabulary.

## Do not execute yet

At filing time, five parallel Execute agents (tickets 0688, 0689, 0690,
0691, 0694) are actively working inside `bench/sdt-sitter/` paths across
several branches. Moving the directory now would break every one of them.
Execute this only once that wave (and its Wave B follow-up, 0692/0693/0695/
0696) has fully merged -- check `tickets/closed/` for all of 0688-0696
before starting.

## Work

- `git mv bench/sdt-sitter plugins/sdt-sitter` (preserves history).
- Update every path reference: `Makefile` targets, `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`,
  `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs`, `bench/build_sdt_sitter.py` (or move it
  too, to `plugins/sdt-sitter/build.py`), any `verification/*.md` or
  `verification/probes/sdt-sitter-harness/` reference to the old path, and
  README's own file listing if it names `bench/` explicitly.
- Grep the whole repo for the literal string `bench/sdt-sitter` after the
  move and confirm zero hits outside git history/DECISIONS.md/tickets.
- No behavior change -- this is a pure path move. `make check` must be
  byte-identical in outcome before and after (same tests, same pass count).

## Acceptance

- [x] `plugins/sdt-sitter/` exists with full git history preserved
      (`git log --follow` on any file inside it shows pre-move commits) --
      reaches 5572dcf, the sitter's first commit.
- [x] `bench/sdt-sitter/` no longer exists.
- [x] Before this review follow-up, `make check` ran green on the path move at
      1038 passed, 14 skipped. Against the 1048-test baseline, that branch
      state added four tests: `tests/test_check_sitter_version.py` (1),
      `tests/test_check_models.py` (2), and
      `tests/test_index_driver_roster_closure.py` (1).
- [x] This review follow-up adds two `tests/test_check_progress.py` controls
      for the newly admitted `plugins/` repo-path root; `python3 -m pytest
      tests/test_check_progress.py -q` passes (50 passed).
- [x] No remaining reference to the old path anywhere in the tracked tree,
      outside git history, DECISIONS.md, tickets -- and `HOMES` in
      `bench/check_sitter_version.py`, which must name it: the pre-move
      payload history is read through it.
